        "header": "1Introduction",
        "images": [
            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.22264/2610.22264v1/figure_1_updated.png",
                "caption": "Figure 1:Comparison of uniform token weighting in GRPO and semantic span weighting in SCOPE.A T2I evaluator provides a single reward for the image. Standard GRPO derives an advantage for the completion and applies it across token positions. However, compositional prompt edits are naturally organized into semantic phrases whose boundaries need not align with tokenizer positions.SCOPEpreserves the same advantage for the completion and derives a shared coefficient for each semantic span from shifts in policy log probabilities. This coefficient modulates all token updates within the span.",
                "position": 266
            }
        ]
